{% chat role: "system" %}
You label the pages of a book one by one, judging each page on its own. Then you give one guess for the whole book.
{% endchat %}

{% chat role: "user" %}
{% if every_page %}The book has {{ page_count }} pages; every page is shown below{% else %}The book has {{ page_count }} pages. You are shown {{ pages.size }} of them: the first {{ opening_count }}, {{ middle_count }} spread through the middle, and the last {{ end_count }}{% endif %}, each as a small image with its first 300 characters of text.

Label each page shown.

Page type:
- cover: Front or back cover.
- front-matter: Title page, copyright, contents, or a preface, foreword or introduction written about the book by its author, editor or publisher.
- story: Narrative: tells a story (fiction or tale), as prose or as text with illustrations.
- lesson: Teaches a topic to learners: explanations, examples, worked content addressed to students.
- exercise: Tasks for the reader to do: questions to answer, blanks, matching, circling, writing.
- informational: Factual or academic prose read for information, not a lesson: article, paper, report, manual.
- back-matter: Credits, licence, index, glossary, about the author, list of other titles.
- blank: Empty or nearly empty page, or a picture with no text that does not carry a story.

Text placement:
- on-art: On the picture. {% render "_setup_recommender_words", where: "on-picture" %}
- beside-art: Beside the picture. {% render "_setup_recommender_words", where: "beside-picture" %}
- text-only: Mostly text; pictures small or absent.
- no-text: No readable text.

meaningfulFigure: true when the page has a diagram, chart, map, table, labelled figure or infographic whose labels carry meaning (not a plain photo or illustration).

Finally, bookGenre: what the whole book most likely is (story, textbook or reference), judging from everything shown, including what any preface says about the book.

{% for page in pages -%}
Page {{ page.number }}: Text: {{ page.text | default: "(no text)" }}

{% endfor -%}
{% for page in pages %}{% if page.image != "" %}
Page {{ page.number }}:
{% image page.image %}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% endchat %}
